  "details": "The new FBT calibration effectively requires a mirror to be able to align legs\nPreviously this wasn't an issue as the user could look down to see their avatars legs, but with how the avatar now follows your head, this is no longer possible\nAs a proposal, locally spawn a mirror in front of the user during calibration to allow the user to align their legs in locations that lack a mirror.\nAn alternative would be to show a clone of the avatar along with your tracker balls, which might be more performant\nWhatever solution is used, (mirror or clone) should also draw over the surrounding environment to provide the ability to calibrate in cramped spaces",
